# CVS Engine Project Rules

This repository builds reusable ML experiment infrastructure for AI-assisted Critical View of Safety scoring research in laparoscopic cholecystectomy.

## Architecture (canonical intent)

- **One repository**, one shared Python package (`src/cvs_engine/`), with **two independently executable stages**.
- Each stage has its own entrypoint, configuration, output artifacts, and execution report. Shared logic stays in the existing dataset, model, task, training, evaluation, and utility packages.
- **Stage 1** uses a **frozen pretrained visual encoder**, caches embeddings, aggregates image embeddings per case, and trains a prediction head (and optional trainable aggregation). Stage 1 includes predictor training; it is not feature extraction alone.
- **Stage 2** adapts the encoder through fine-tuning with appropriate prediction/aggregation modules, using original images and Stage 1 handoff artifacts.
- A thin stage orchestration layer (for example `src/cvs_engine/stages/`) is **proposed only** until an approved milestone creates it. Do not invent executable stage entrypoints ahead of approval.

Canonical detail lives in `.ai/00_project_reference.md` and `.ai/01_implementation_roadmap.md`.

## Milestone discipline

- Implement **only** the milestone approved in `.ai/90_current_milestone.md`.
- Prefer small, bounded changes. Do not expand into the next milestone “while you are here.”
- Clearly separate **implemented** behavior from **planned / proposed** functionality in docs and reports.
- After implementation, update `.ai/91_implementation_report.md` with changed files, summary, verification evidence, limitations, and intentionally not implemented items.
- Review findings belong in `.ai/92_review_report.md`; corrections in `.ai/93_corrections.md`. Do not declare human/independent review acceptance in implementation reports.

## Safety and scope

- Do not make clinical claims.
- Research experiment outputs only; no medical decision support, patient-facing guidance, or live-surgery advice.
- Do not add real datasets, VLMs, SAM-2, Optuna, MLflow, advanced UI, cloud setup, or production deployment unless explicitly approved in the current milestone.
- The Streamlit UI is a minimal local visibility layer, not a production dashboard.
- Both stages must eventually support CLI execution without launching Streamlit (when stage milestones authorize that work).

## Engineering defaults

- Keep the code Linux/DGX-ready and WSL2/Ubuntu-friendly.
- Use Poetry for dependency management (Python 3.11).
- Keep the project config-driven and testable.
- Future functionality changes must include meaningful tests for introduced behavior, relevant failure cases, and affected integration boundaries.
- Always report changed files and verification results.
- Prefer `poetry run python -m pytest`, `poetry run ruff check .`, and `poetry run pyright` as the quality baseline.

